                        C h e s s w i z  1.0

=====================================================================

Website: https://chesswizapp.com

Chesswiz is an advanced, high-performance chess database application
for Linux, Windows, and macOS, version 1.0. It provides a complete
desktop environment for chess players, coaches, and researchers to
manage game archives, analyze positions with powerful chess engines,
train openings, and review games.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Key Features
---------------------------------------------------------------------

* Databases
  - High-performance native database engine (.sci) handling collections
    of millions of games with instant search, filtering, and database
    switching.
  - Comprehensive PGN (Portable Game Notation) support with UTF-8
    encoding enabled by default.
  - Rich game browsing and editing with variation trees, text
    annotations, and standard evaluation marks.
  - Database maintenance suite: duplicate game detection, integrity
    verification, opening tree statistics, and database compacting.
  - Flexible search capabilities: header filters, material search,
    positional and pattern searches, and rating criteria.
  - Player preparation reports and opponent dossiers featuring opening
    tendencies, recent games, and tailored prep working sets.
  - Correspondence chess management: live clock displays, automated
    move timestamping, game list manager, and ICCF XFCC server sync.

* Engines
  - Bundled high-performance chess engines: Stockfish, Reckless, and
    Sjeng.
  - Full support for external UCI and WinBoard protocol engines with
    customizable thread, memory, and search profiles.
  - Automated engine matches and tournament testing.

* Analysis
  - Real-time interactive analysis with multi-PV line evaluation and
    search depth indicators.
  - Automated game review and tactical blunder alerts highlighting
    mistakes and missed opportunities.
  - Integrated endgame tablebase probing with Syzygy 3-4-5-6 piece
    tablebases.
  - Visual evaluation charts and score progression graphs.

* 3D Board
  - Interactive hardware-accelerated 3D board view with photorealistic
    materials (Classic Woodcraft and Photorealistic Walnut & Maple).
  - Customizable piece sets, square styles, camera angles, lighting,
    and smooth board rotation.

* Media
  - Integrated multimedia playback panel supporting synchronized audio
    and video streams (MP4 and web streams).
  - Interactive training lessons linking video timestamps directly to
    moves and board positions.

* Assistant That Runs the App for You
  - Built-in AI assistant that operates application features for you:
    executes queries, loads games, sets up board positions, annotates
    moves, and generates study plans from natural language requests.
  - Keyboard-accessible drawer with intelligent command routing.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Installation
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Linux:
   Install the official Debian/Ubuntu package:

      sudo dpkg -i chesswiz_1.0_*.deb

   or run portable builds directly from the source tree.

Windows:
   Run the Windows installer setup:

      Chesswiz-1.0-setup.exe

   The installer registers file associations for .sci and .pgn files
   and creates Start Menu and desktop shortcuts. Portable ZIP archives
   are also available; extract and launch tkchesswiz.exe.

macOS:
   Download the Chesswiz.app application bundle (macOS 11.0 or later,
   Universal binary supporting Apple Silicon and Intel):

      Drag Chesswiz.app into your /Applications folder and launch.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
Build from Source
---------------------------------------------------------------------

Requirements: a C++11 compiler, Tcl/Tk 8.6 development files, and the
system libraries listed below. On Debian/Ubuntu/Mint:

   sudo apt-get install build-essential tcl8.6 tk8.6 tcl8.6-dev tk8.6-dev \
     libfreetype6-dev libsm-dev libxcursor-dev libfontconfig1-dev \
     libgdbm-dev libexpat1-dev libmpv-dev libzzip-dev zlib1g-dev

Then, from the root of this source tree:

   ./configure
   make

This compiles the C++ backend in src/ and bundles the Tcl interface into
tcl/chesswiz.

To run immediately from the build tree:

   src/tkchesswiz -encoding utf-8 tcl/chesswiz

To install system-wide (use --prefix with configure to customize):

   sudo make install

Windows and macOS packaging scripts are located in scripts/ (see
docs/dev/PORT_WINDOWS_MAC_SPEC.md).

